  "worked_solution": "We can calculate the surface area of a cylinder using the formula\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {r}^{2}+2\\pi rh,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius and $h$ is the height of the cylinder.\n\nSubstituting $r=21\\,\\text{in}$ and $h=30\\,\\text{in}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi (21)^{2}+2\\pi (21)(30) \\\\  & =882\\pi +1\\,260\\pi  \\\\  & =2\\,142\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
